    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9286" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comma</span></b> , ătis, n., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμμα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gram. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A division of a period</i> (in <i><span class="en">Cic. Or.
				62, 211</span></i>; <i><span class="en">66, 223</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				4, 22</span></i>, written as Greek; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pure Lat. incisum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					1, 8, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Diom. 2, p. 460 sq.</span></i>
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A mark of punctuation</i>, <i>a
			comma</i>, Don. p. 1742 P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In verse, <i>the
			cœsura</i>, Marc. Vict. p. 2519 P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
